{
  "title": "A late, unrepaired amount change freezes -- even after a challenge already passed",
  "description": "This call originates from a registered device in the wrong city for Dana's SSO session, so identity fails from the start even though the request itself first looks clean and one verification challenge is passed. Then, unprompted, she changes the wire amount with no correction language and no explanation -- a fresh, unrepaired contradiction on a critical field. By design (see rules.ts), a freeze-eligible call is allowed to act on a still-unconfirmed critical value rather than loop forever asking for readback confirmation (the fail-safe direction), so this does not stall at another round of questions: it FREEZEs (rule 7b, a contradiction alongside a failed check). The re-priced amount also no longer matches the scheduled payment, so context fails too by the end -- this file happens to also clear the tally>=3 bar (7c) at the same time; see task-6-report.md for why an amount drift naturally drags context down with it, and which OTHER corpus files isolate a bare 7b more cleanly.",
